course: dictionary
lesson: 4850
title: Hyperactive and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Hyperactive» means much more active than normal, so you cannot keep still or stay calm. Look at the clues around it: «Lively» on a school report often means disruptive or hyperactive. Lively sounds nice, but disruptive means causing trouble, so hyperactive means someone who cannot settle.
explain: Doctors also use the word in a serious way. Hyperactivity is a part of ADHD, a condition that makes it hard for some people to sit still and concentrate. Talk about it kindly, because it is about how a person's brain works, not about being naughty.
explain: People also use the word as a joke. «Live wire» means a very energetic, hyperactive child, one so full of energy that he cannot keep still. Ask yourself: is the sentence serious, or is it teasing? The clues tell you which.
fact: Hyperactive means much more active than normal.
fact: Hyperactivity is a part of ADHD, a condition that makes it hard for some people to sit still and concentrate.
fact: «Feeling hyper» is informal, and it is used about someone very excited, like after a party.
fact: Careful studies find that sugar does not make most children hyperactive; excitement at parties is a likelier reason.
fact: Too much sugar at once can make you feel sick, even though it does not make most children hyperactive.
exercise: «Lively» on a school report often means disruptive or hyperactive. What does hyperactive mean here? | Very quiet and calm | Neat and tidy | Hungry and tired | *Much more active than normal, unable to keep still
exercise: A friend says, «You're so hyper after that party!» What does hyper mean? | Angry at everyone | Bored in class | Tired and sleepy | *Very excited and full of energy
exercise: Studies show sugar does not make most children hyperactive. What do careful studies find about sugar? | Sugar stops children feeling excited | Sugar makes children clever | *Sugar does not make most children hyperactive | Sugar always makes children hyperactive
test: In a health lesson, «hyperactivity» is a part of which condition? | *ADHD | Asthma | Measles | Flu
test: What does «hyperactive» mean in «a hyperactive child»? | Very clean and tidy | Very quiet at school | Very tired and slow | *Much more active than normal, unable to keep still
exam: In «Live wire» means a very energetic, hyperactive child, what is the author doing? | Explaining a serious medical fact | Describing a sleepy cat | Giving a rule about sugar | *Using a joking, informal way to describe a very energetic child
